Eight of the nine are uncategorized; the only unused template is <code>Template:BITwiki</code>. <code>Template:Infobox</code> is categorized under <code>Concepts</code> and is used across constitutional, epistemic, ontology, schema, governance, migration and validation documents.

=== The Infobox discrepancy ===
The live <code>Template:Infobox</code> renders title, type, status, related implementation and category. Later V1 pages pass many additional parameters such as description, author, version, epistemic status, confidence, workflow and ontology. Those parameters express important '''design intent''', but the actual live template does not consume most of them.

V2 must therefore recover the intended schema from the writings without pretending V1 already implemented it.

=== Wanted templates ===
<code>Special:WantedTemplates</code> contains '''59 referenced-but-uncreated templates'''. <code>Template:Documentation</code> alone has 82 references; other wanted titles represent planned document-header, epistemic-marker, schema-matter, infobox, portal, citation and validation machinery.

Wanted templates are design-intent evidence, not deployed V1 objects and not an automatic V2 implementation backlog.

== Categories: membership without category pages ==
V1 uses '''162 distinct category names''', but the Category namespace contains '''zero created category pages'''. Every V1 category is therefore a membership/index label without authored Category-page documentation.

The archive preserves every category name, count and member in <code>archive-v1/categories/</code>. See [[BITwiki:V1 category migration]] for the functional refactor.

=== Category:BITwiki Templates ===
This category has exactly seven members, but all seven are Main-namespace template-system documentation pages rather than actual Template namespace objects. See [[BITwiki:Templates and categories]].

== Semantic implementation ==
V1 contains extensive Main-namespace documentation for properties, entity types, relationships, ontology alignment, SMW templates and Lua modules. The actual namespace implementation is much smaller.

=== Property namespace ===
Only four authored Property pages exist, all imported vocabulary:
* <code>Property:Foaf:homepage</code>
* <code>Property:Foaf:knows</code>
* <code>Property:Foaf:name</code>
* <code>Property:Owl:differentFrom</code>

Semantic annotations in Main pages may create implicit SMW properties; they are not equivalent to authored <code>Property:</code> definition pages.

=== smw/schema ===
Three pages exist:
* <code>smw/schema:Group:Predefined properties</code>
* <code>smw/schema:Group:Schema properties</code>
* <code>smw/schema:Profile:Facetedsearch default profile</code>

=== Concept / Module ===
No Concept namespace pages and no Module namespace pages exist in the archived public V1 snapshot. Documentation describing concepts/Lua modules is therefore design/specification material unless an implementation exists elsewhere.

== MediaWiki configuration ==
Six MediaWiki pages exist:
* <code>MediaWiki:Common.css</code>
* <code>MediaWiki:KnowledgeGraphOptions</code>
* four SMW imported-vocabulary configuration pages for FOAF, OWL, schema and SKOS.

== File archive ==
V1 has two File description pages and two corresponding file revision metadata records:
* <code>File:Binary bitwiki logo.png</code>
* <code>File:Wikiteq.png</code>

Their File-page wikitext and revision histories are archived. MediaWiki still reports the original upload metadata—including timestamps, byte sizes, dimensions, SHA-1 values and upload URLs—but both historical PNG URLs now return 404 from both the API-reported <code>/w/images/</code> path and the current <code>/images/</code> fallback.

Therefore:
* file revision metadata accounted for: '''2 / 2''';
* binary files retrievable/captured: '''0 / 2''';
* historical binary references preserved as unavailable: '''2 / 2'''.

The archive records this explicitly in <code>archive-v1/files/index.json</code>. It does not fabricate the missing binaries or call them captured.

